    <main id="main">
        <div class="hero">
            <h1>Services Layer: Domain Business Logic</h1>
            <p>Domain services encapsulate entity-specific business logic. All 15+ services inherit from CommonService and implement CRUD, state transitions, and multi-tenant isolation.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="intro-box">
            <strong>Analogy:</strong> If the db/ layer is a "filing cabinet," then services are "job roles" in a company. A DocumentService is like a "Document Manager"—they know how to create, retrieve, update, and delete documents correctly. They know which documents are deleted, which belong to which tenant, and what the rules are for naming and organizing. Handlers (API endpoints) ask services to do work, rather than directly accessing the filing cabinet.
        </div>
        
        <h2>Purpose & Architecture</h2>
        
        <p>The <code>services/</code> layer contains business logic for each domain entity:</p>
        
        <ul>
            <li><strong>CommonService Base Class:</strong> All services inherit from CommonService, providing shared methods: pagination, tenant filtering, error handling, logging.</li>
            <li><strong>15+ Domain Services:</strong> Each service manages one or more related entities (DocumentService manages Document + file uploads, DialogService manages Dialog definitions, etc.).</li>
            <li><strong>State Transition Management:</strong> Services handle complex state machines (e.g., Task: pending → processing → done/error). Handlers never directly update entity state.</li>
            <li><strong>Atomic Operations:</strong> Services coordinate multi-step operations (create document + queue task, create conversation + send welcome message) atomically.</li>
            <li><strong>Soft Delete Coordination:</strong> Services enforce soft-delete semantics globally (queries filter deleted_at.is_null(), restore operations reset deleted_at).</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Common Service Base Class</h2>
        
        <p>All services inherit from <code>CommonService</code> in <code>common_service.py</code>:</p>
        
        <pre><code>class CommonService:
    '''Base class for all domain services.'''
    
    def __init__(self):
        self._logger = logging.getLogger(self.__class__.__name__)
    
    def get_by_id(self, id: str, tenant_id: str = None):
        '''Retrieve entity by ID with optional tenant check.'''
        entity = Entity.get_by_id(id)
        if tenant_id and entity.tenant_id != tenant_id:
            raise TenantMismatch(f"Entity {id} not in tenant {tenant_id}")
        return entity
    
    def list_by_tenant(self, tenant_id: str, offset=0, limit=50):
        '''Paginated list for tenant.'''
        return Entity.select().where(
            Entity.tenant_id == tenant_id,
            Entity.deleted_at.is_null()
        ).offset(offset).limit(limit)
    
    def delete(self, id: str, tenant_id: str):
        '''Soft delete with tenant check.'''
        entity = self.get_by_id(id, tenant_id)
        entity.deleted_at = datetime.now()
        entity.save()
        return entity
</code></pre>
        
